{
  "title": "49: al-Hojoraat الحجرات",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تُقَدِّمُوْا بَيْنَ يَدَىِ اللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ وَ اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(1)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA WA BAYNA YADAA LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI WA TAQUL LAAH INNAL LAAHA SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nO you who believe! be not forward in the presence of Allah and His Apostle, and be careful of (your duty to) Allah; surely Allah is Hearing, Knowing. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَرْفَعُوْۤا اَصْوَاتَكُمْ فَوْقَ صَوْتِ النَّبِىِّ وَلَا تَجْهَرُوْا لَهٗ بِالْقَوْلِ كَجَهْرِ بَعْضِكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ اَنْ تَحْبَطَ اَعْمَالُكُمْ وَاَنْتُمْ لَا تَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(2)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TARFAU’OOA AASWAATAKUM FAWQA SAWTE NESAAA-AN WA LAA TAJHAROOA LAHU BIL-QAWLE KAJAHRE BAA’ZEKUM LE-BA’ZIN AN TAHBATA A-A’MAALOKUM WA ANTUM LAA TASH-O’ROON.\nO you who believe! do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet, and do not speak loud to him as you speak loud to one another, lest your deeds became null while you do not perceive. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَغُضُّوْنَ اَصْوَاتَهُمْ عِنْدَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ اُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ امْتَحَنَ اللّٰهُ قُلُوْبَهُمْ لِلتَّقْوٰىؕ لَهُمْ مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَّاَجْرٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(3)\nINNAL LAZEENA YAGHUZZOONA AASWAATAHUM I’NDAL RASOOLIL LAAHE OOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA AMTAHANA LAAHO QULOOBAHUM LIT-TAQWAA LAHUM MAGHFERATUNW WA AJRUN A’ZEEM.\nSurely those who lower their voices before Allah's Apostle are they whose hearts Allah has proved for guarding (against evil); they shall have forgiveness and a great reward. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يُنَادُوْنَكَ مِنْ وَّرَآءِ الْحُجُرٰتِ اَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(4)\nINNAL LAZEENA YUNAADOONAKA MIN FAS-ALOOHUNNA AL-HUJURAATE AKSAROHUM LAA YA’QELOON.\n(As for) those who call out to you from behind the private chambers, surely most of them do not understand. \nوَلَوْ اَنَّهُمْ صَبَرُوْا حَتّٰى تَخْرُجَ اِلَيْهِمْ لَكَانَ خَيْرًا لَّهُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(5)\nWA LAW ANNAHUM SABAROO HATTAA TAKHRUJA ELAYHIM LAKAANA KHAYRAN LAHUM WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nAnd if they wait patiently until you come out to them, it would certainly be better for them, and Allah is Forgiving, Merciful. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنْ جَآءَكُمْ فَاسِقٌ ۢ بِنَبَاٍ فَتَبَيَّنُوْۤا اَنْ تُصِيْبُوْا قَوْمًا ۢ بِجَهَالَةٍ فَتُصْبِحُوْا عَلٰى مَا فَعَلْتُمْ نٰدِمِيْنَ‏(6)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO IN JAAA-AKUM FAASEQUN BENABAIYN FATABAYNOOA AN TUSEEBOOA QAWMAN BEJAHAALATIN FATUSBEHOOA A’LAA MAA FAA’ALTUM NAADEMEENA.\nO you who believe! if an evil-doer comes to you with a report, look carefully into it, lest you harm a people in ignorance, then be sorry for what you have done. \nوَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ فِيْكُمْ رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِؕ لَوْ يُطِيْعُكُمْ فِىْ كَثِيْرٍ مِّنَ الْاَمْرِ لَعَنِتُّمْ وَ لٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ حَبَّبَ اِلَيْكُمُ الْاِيْمَانَ وَزَيَّنَهٗ فِىْ قُلُوْبِكُمْ وَكَرَّهَ اِلَيْكُمُ الْكُفْرَ وَالْفُسُوْقَ وَالْعِصْيَانَؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الرّٰشِدُوْنَۙ‏(7)\nWA’ LAMOO ANNAL FEEKUM TOAZOO LAAH LAW YUTEEU’UKUM FEE KASEERIM MENAL AL-AAMRE LAA’ANETTUM WA LAAKENNA LAAHA HABBABA AELAYKUMU EEMAANA WAZAYNAH FEE QOLOOBEKUM WAKARRAHA AELAYKUMU KUFRA WAL FUSOOQA WAL E’ESYAANA OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL AR-RAASHEDOONA.\nAnd know that among you is Allah's Apostle; should he obey you in many a matter, you would surely fall into distress, but Allah has endeared the faith to you and has made it seemly in your hearts, and He has made hateful to you unbelief and transgression and disobedience; these it is that are the followers of a right way. \nفَضْلًا مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَنِعْمَةً  ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(8)\nFAZLAM MENAL LAAHE WANEA’MATAN WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nBy grace from Allah and as a favor; and Allah is Knowing, Wise. \nوَاِنْ طَآئِفَتٰنِ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اقْتَتَلُوْا فَاَصْلِحُوْا بَيْنَهُمَاۚ فَاِنْۢ بَغَتْ اِحْدٰٮهُمَا عَلَى الْاُخْرٰى فَقَاتِلُوا الَّتِىْ تَبْغِىْ حَتّٰى تَفِىْٓءَ اِلٰٓى اَمْرِ اللّٰهِ ۚ فَاِنْ فَآءَتْ فَاَصْلِحُوْا بَيْنَهُمَا بِالْعَدْلِ وَاَقْسِطُوْا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُقْسِطِيْنَ‏(9)\nWA TAAEFATAANE MENAL MOAMENEEN TATALOO WA FAASLEHOOA BAYNAHOMAA FA-IN BAGHAT UKHRAA A’LAL AL-AUKHRAA FAQAATELOOA LATEE TABGHEAA HATTAA TAFEAAAAA ELAA AMRE LAAHE FA-IN FAAAT FAASLEHOOA BAYNAHOMAA BIL-A’DL WAAQSETOOA INNAL LAAHA YOHIBBUL AL-MUQSETEENA.\nAnd if two parties of the believers quarrel, make peace between them; but if one of them acts wrongfully towards the other, fight that which acts wrongfully until it returns to Allah's command; then if it returns, make peace between them with justice and act equitably; surely Allah loves those who act equitably. \nاِنَّمَا الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ اِخْوَةٌ فَاَصْلِحُوْا بَيْنَ اَخَوَيْكُمْ ۚوَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُوْنَ ‏(10)\nINNAMAA MOAMENOONA AEKHWATUN FAASLEHOOA BAYNA AAKHAWAYKUM WAT TAQUL LAAHA LA-A’LLAKUM TURHAMOON.\nThe believers are but brethren, therefore make peace between your brethren and be careful of (your duty to) Allah that mercy may be had on you. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا يَسْخَرْ قَوْمٌ مِّنْ قَوْمٍ عَسٰٓى اَنْ يَّكُوْنُوْا خَيْرًا مِّنْهُمْ وَلَا نِسَآءٌ مِّنْ نِّسَآءٍ عَسٰٓى اَنْ يَّكُنَّ خَيْرًا مِّنْهُنَّۚ وَلَا تَلْمِزُوْۤا اَنْفُسَكُمْ وَلَا تَنَابَزُوْا بِالْاَلْقَابِؕ بِئْسَ الِاسْمُ الْفُسُوْقُ بَعْدَ الْاِيْمَانِ ۚ وَمَنْ لَّمْ يَتُبْ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(11)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA YASKHAR QAWMUN MIN QAWMIN A’SAA AN YYAKOONOOA KHAYRAN MINHUM WA LAA NESAAUN MIN NNESAAIN A’SAA AN YYAKUNNA KHAYRAN MIN-HUNNA WA LAA TALMEZOOA ANFOSAKUM WA LAA TANAABAZOOA BIL-AALQAABE MASALUL ALEASMU AL-FUSOOQU BA’DA AL-AEEMAANE WA MAN LAM YATUB FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL ZAALEMOON.\nO you who believe! let not (one) people laugh at (another) people perchance they may be better than they, nor let women (laugh) at (other) women, perchance they may be better than they; and do not find fault with your own people nor call one another by nicknames; evil is a bad name after faith, and whoever does not turn, these it is that are the unjust. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اجْتَنِبُوْا كَثِيْرًا مِّنَ الظَّنِّ اِنَّ بَعْضَ الظَّنِّ اِثْمٌ وَّلَا تَجَسَّسُوْا وَلَا يَغْتَبْ بَّعْضُكُمْ بَعْضًا ؕ اَ يُحِبُّ اَحَدُكُمْ اَنْ يَّاْكُلَ لَحْمَ اَخِيْهِ مَيْتًا فَكَرِهْتُمُوْهُ ؕ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ تَوَّابٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(12)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANUT AJTANEBOOA KASEERAA MENAL AZ-ZANNE INNAL YAWM AZ-ZANNE ISMUN WA LAA TAJASSASOOA WA LAA YAGHTAB BBAA’ZUKUM BA’ZAN AAYUHEBBU AHADOKUM AN YYAAKULA LAHMA AKHEEHE MAYTAN FAKAREHTUMOOHU WAT TAQUL LAAHA INNAL LAAHA TAWABUN RAHEEM.\nO you who believe! avoid most of suspicion, for surely suspicion in some cases is a sin, and do not spy nor let some of you backbite others. Does one of you like to eat the flesh of his dead brother? But you abhor it; and be careful of (your duty to) Allah, surely Allah is Oft-returning (to mercy), Merciful. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اِنَّا خَلَقْنٰكُمْ مِّنْ ذَكَرٍ وَّاُنْثٰى وَجَعَلْنٰكُمْ شُعُوْبًا وَّقَبَآئِلَ لِتَعَارَفُوْا ؕ اِنَّ اَكْرَمَكُمْ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ اَ تْقٰٮكُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلِيْمٌ خَبِيْرٌ‏(13)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO INNAA KHALAQNAAKUM MIN ZAKARIN WWAANSAA WA JA-A’LNAAKUM SHUU’OOBAN WWAQABAAELA LETAA’AARAFOOA INNAL AAKRAMAKUM I’NDAL LAAHE AATQAAKUM INNAL LAAHA A’LEEM KHABEERUM.\nO you men! surely We have created you of a male and a female, and made you tribes and families that you may know each other; surely the most honorable of you with Allah is the one among you most careful (of his duty); surely Allah is Knowing, Aware. \nقَالَتِ الْاَعْرَابُ اٰمَنَّا ؕ قُلْ لَّمْ تُؤْمِنُوْا وَلٰكِنْ قُوْلُوْۤا اَسْلَمْنَا وَلَمَّا يَدْخُلِ الْاِيْمَانُ فِىْ قُلُوْبِكُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ تُطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ لَا يَلِتْكُمْ مِّنْ اَعْمَالِكُمْ شَيْئًا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(14)\nQAALATE AL-AAA’RAABU AAMANNAA QUL LAM LAM TOAMENOO WA LAAKIL QOOLOOA AASLAMNAA WA LAMMAA YADKHULE AL-AEEMAANU FEE QOLOOBEKUM WA TUTEEU’OOA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU LAA YALETKUM MIN AAA’MAALEKUM SHAY-ANW INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nThe dwellers of the desert say: We believe. Say: You do not believe but say, We submit; and faith has not yet entered into your hearts; and if you obey Allah and His Apostle, He will not diminish aught of your deeds; surely Allah is Forgiving, Merciful. \nاِنَّمَا الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَرْتَابُوْا وَجَاهَدُوْا بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الصّٰدِقُوْنَ‏(15)\nINNAMAA MOAMENOONA LAZEENA AAMANOO BIL-LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI SUMMA LAM YARTAABOOA WA JAAHADOO BEAAMWAALEHEM WA ANFOSEHIM FEE SABEELIL LAAHE OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL SAADEQOON.\nThe believers are only those who believe in Allah and His Apostle then they doubt not and struggle hard with their wealth and their lives in the way of Allah; they are the truthful ones. \nقُلْ اَ تُعَلِّمُوْنَ اللّٰهَ بِدِيْنِكُمْ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(16)\nQUL AATUA’ALLEMOONA LAAHA BE-DEENEKUM WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ WAL LAAHO BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nSay: Do you apprise Allah of your religion, and Allah knows what is in the heavens and what is in the earth; and Allah is Cognizant of all things. \nيَمُنُّوْنَ عَلَيْكَ اَنْ اَسْلَمُوْا ؕ قُلْ لَّا تَمُنُّوْا عَلَىَّ اِسْلَامَكُمْ ۚ بَلِ اللّٰهُ يَمُنُّ عَلَيْكُمْ اَنْ هَدٰٮكُمْ لِلْاِيْمَانِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(17)\nYAMUNNOONA A’LAYKA AN AASLAMOOA QUL LAA TAMUNNOOA A’LAYYA AESLAAMAKUM BALIL LAAHO YAMUNNU A’LAYKUM AN HADAAKUM LIL-AEEMAANE IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nThey think that they lay you under an obligation by becoming Muslims. Say: Lay me not under obligation by your Islam: rather Allah lays you under an obligation by guiding you to the faith if you are truthful. \nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ غَيْبَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ وَاللّٰهُ بَصِيْرٌۢ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(18)\nINNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO GHAYBAS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ WAL LAAHO BASEER BEMAA TA’MALOON.\nSurely Allah knows the unseen things of the heavens and the earth; and Allah sees what you do. ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Hojoraat (The Chambers)\nThis Surah was revealed in Madinah and it has 18 verses. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the reward for reciting this Surah can be compared to ten times the number of believers and disbelievers on Earth.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has narrated that those who recite this Surah will be counted from among those who visited the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.). Writing this Surah and keeping it in one’s possession makes the Shaitan run away and acts as a protection in times of war and unrest. If a pregnant woman drinks water in which this Surah has been dissolved, then both herself and her child will remain safe from danger and drinking this water also increases breast-milk in a breastfeeding mother."
}
